{
  "name": "305. xAI image generation and edit on the Bifrost–Tokun contract (xai image contract)",
  "description": "Pins TXE-6606 (contract C4, C5, C6) for xai on every route that reaches its image methods: /v1/images/generations (JSON), /v1/images/edits (JSON and multipart), the OpenAI integration routes /openai/v1/images/generations (JSON) and /openai/v1/images/edits (multipart), and the async routes /v1/async/images/generations and /v1/async/images/edits, which parse with the same functions as the sync routes and run the same provider methods from the async executor (each GET case polls its job until it is completed or failed, up to 40 lookups about 3 s apart, and fails if it is still running; a refused job is failed with the 400 and the full error). quality reaches xAI on grok-imagine-image-2.0, the only model xAI documents as taking it, and is refused with 400 caller_unsupported_parameter (error.param quality) on any other model; deferred is refused (error.param deferred) because the sync image routes make one upstream call; an edit is sent to xAI's JSON /v1/images/edits whatever the inbound shape (before the change xai answered image edit as an unsupported operation), an uploaded file becoming a data URI, and a price-affecting field xAI's edit has no counterpart for, such as size, is refused; a resolution tier xAI does not offer (4K) is refused, which on /openai/v1/images/edits also pins that the multipart parser now carries resolution (before the change it was dropped and the edit billed at xAI's default tier). A successful response carries usage.vendor_cost {amount: cost_in_usd_ticks, unit: usd_ticks} and usage.output_images equal to the delivered images. The refusal cases make no upstream call and cost nothing; the 200 cases are paid (one 1k image each). Unit tests pin the wire bodies: core/providers/xai/xai_test.go for the provider, transports/bifrost-http/handlers (inference_test.go, inference_imageedit_test.go) and integrations/openai_test.go from each route's parser to xAI's wire.",
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "[EXPECT-400] /v1/images/generations - xai/grok-imagine-image with quality is refused, the model does not take it (xai image contract)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('quality on grok-imagine-image is refused with caller_unsupported_parameter before any upstream call', function () {",
              "  var t = pm.response.text();",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.code, 'expected 400; got: ' + t.slice(0, 400)).to.equal(400);",
              "  var j = pm.response.json();",
              "  pm.expect(j.extra_fields && j.extra_fields.error_type, 'error_type: ' + t.slice(0, 400)).to.equal('caller_unsupported_parameter');",
              "  pm.expect(j.error && j.error.param, 'error.param: ' + t.slice(0, 400)).to.equal('quality');",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"model\": \"xai/grok-imagine-image\",\n  \"prompt\": \"a red apple on a white table\",\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"quality\": \"low\"\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/images/generations",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "v1",
            "images",
            "generations"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
